{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 1',lv:'U',n:1,q:"What is a golden vector?",say:'Question one. What is a golden vector?',cues:{k:'Question one',q:'What is a golden'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 1',lv:'U',n:1,q:"What is a golden vector?",say:'It is a known-correct pair of inputs and output, used as the expected value in a checker. It comes from a truth table, a reference model, or a known-good simulation.',cues:{a1:'It is a known',a2:'It comes from'},al:[["A known-correct input-output pair, used as the expected value in a checker.",'a1'],["It comes from a truth table, a reference model or a known-good simulation.",'a2']],vis:(c,u,b)=>{let s='';
 s+=g('pop',tk(c,'a1'),lsT(20,40,'one golden vector',{fs:26,fw:800,fill:GRN})+lsBox(20,64,190,70,{fill:'#E6E9FB',st:BLU,rx:10})+lsT(115,108,'a b s = 1 0 1',{fs:22,a:'middle',m:1,fw:800})+lsAr(212,99,262,99)+
  lsBox(266,64,110,70,{fill:WHT,st:INK,rx:10})+lsT(321,108,'DUT',{fs:26,a:'middle',fw:800})+lsAr(378,99,428,99)+lsT(438,108,'y = 0',{fs:26,m:1,fw:800})+
  lsBox(20,170,190,60,{fill:'#E2F4EC',st:GRN,rx:10})+lsT(115,208,'expected 0',{fs:24,a:'middle',fw:800,fill:GRN})+
  lsBox(266,170,330,60,{fill:'#E2F4EC',st:GRN,rx:10})+lsT(431,208,'y matches: ok ✓',{fs:24,a:'middle',fw:800,fill:GRN}));
 const src=(x,l1,l2)=>lsBox(x,330,186,96,{fill:WHT,st:LSAX,rx:10})+lsT(x+93,l2?370:386,l1,{fs:22,a:'middle',fw:800})+(l2?lsT(x+93,402,l2,{fs:22,a:'middle',fw:800}):'');
 s+=g('pop',tk(c,'a2'),lsT(20,306,'golden vectors come from',{fs:22,fill:LSG})+src(20,'truth table')+src(217,'reference','model')+src(414,'known-good','simulation'));
 return s}},
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 2',lv:'A',n:2,q:"How many bits does a ROM need to implement four functions of 5 inputs?",say:`Question two. How many bits does a ${P('ROM')} need to implement four functions of five inputs?`,cues:{k:'Question two',q:'How many bits'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 2',lv:'A',n:2,q:"How many bits does a ROM need to implement four functions of 5 inputs?",say:'Five inputs address two to the five, thirty-two words. Four functions give four bits per word. Thirty-two times four is one hundred twenty-eight bits.',cues:{fk:'Five inputs address',k1:'two to the five',k2:'Four functions give',k3:'Thirty-two times',k3b:'one hundred twenty-eight'},calc:{f:['ROM size = 2ⁿ words × m bits'],hint:'n = 5 inputs, m = 4 outputs.',fk:'fk',steps:[["Words","2⁵ = 32 words",'k1'],["Bits per word","4 functions: 4 bits",'k2'],["Size",["32 × 4","32 × 4 = 128 bits"],['k3','k3b']]],live:[0,1,2]}},
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 3',lv:'N',n:3,q:"A DUT uses q<=d at posedge clk. The bench uses blocking assignment and reads q at the same posedge. Explain the risk.",say:'Question three. The design under test updates q with a non-blocking assignment at the rising clock edge. The bench uses blocking assignments and reads q at that same edge. Explain the risk.',cues:{k:'Question three',q:'The design under'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 3',lv:'N',n:3,q:"A DUT uses q<=d at posedge clk. The bench uses blocking assignment and reads q at the same posedge. Explain the risk.",say:'It is a race. The bench may read the old q before the non-blocking update lands. Drive the inputs away from the edge, and sample a time unit later, or on the opposite edge.',cues:{a1:'It is a race',a2:'Drive the inputs'},al:[["Race: the bench may read old q before the nonblocking update.",'a1'],["Drive away from the edge; sample after #1 or on the opposite edge.",'a2']],vis:(c,u,b)=>{let s='';
 s+=g('pop',tk(c,'a1'),lsT(20,38,'one time step at posedge clk',{fs:24,fw:800})+
  lsBox(20,58,180,66,{fill:'#E6E9FB',st:BLU,rx:10})+lsT(110,99,'active',{fs:24,a:'middle',fw:800})+lsAr(202,91,226,91)+
  lsBox(230,58,160,66,{fill:'#EEF0F4',st:GRY,rx:10})+lsT(310,99,'inactive',{fs:24,a:'middle',fw:800})+lsAr(392,91,416,91)+
  lsBox(420,58,180,66,{fill:'#FFF1DF',st:ORG,rx:10})+lsT(510,99,'nonblocking',{fs:22,a:'middle',fw:800})+
  lsAr(110,126,110,160,RED,3)+lsT(20,190,'bench reads q: still old',{fs:24,fill:RED,fw:800})+lsAr(510,126,510,206,ORG,3)+lsT(600,236,'q &lt;= d lands here',{fs:24,a:'end',fill:ORG,fw:800,m:1}));
 s+=g('pop',tk(c,'a2'),lsT(20,300,'clk',{fs:22,fill:LSG})+lsWave(70,282,332,90,[0,1,1,0,0,1],BLU,4)+
  `<line x1="190" y1="264" x2="190" y2="352" stroke="${GRN}" stroke-width="4" stroke-dasharray="8 5"/><line x1="340" y1="264" x2="340" y2="352" stroke="${GRN}" stroke-width="4" stroke-dasharray="8 5"/>`+
  lsT(190,392,'sample #1 later',{fs:24,a:'middle',fill:GRN,fw:800,m:1})+lsT(380,440,'or at the opposite edge',{fs:24,a:'middle',fill:GRN,fw:800}));
 return s}},
{s:LS,k:'figs',term:'Your notes',title:'For your notes',say:'Your free notes are the PDF linked in the description. Redraw the four vector waveforms and the sixteen bit lookup table from memory.',cues:{t:'Your free notes',f:'Redraw the four'},tags:[["Free notes for this lesson (PDF)", "link in the description"], ["In this lesson", "Test benches and simulation; Programmable logic devices and FPGA architecture"], ["Key terms and glossary", "at the end of the notes"]],figs:[["Four vectors as waveforms", "The mux bench applies a vector at 0, 10, 20 and 30 ns and compares y with the expected 1, 0, 0, 1 ten nanoseconds later, never at the instant the inputs change."], ["The 4-input LUT", "16 configuration bits hold the truth table of f = A·B + C·D; the inputs drive a 16:1 multiplexer, and 1101 reads address 13, which holds 1."]],note:"Sources your free notes draw on: Samir Palnitkar, Verilog HDL (writing test benches); M. Morris Mano and Michael D. Ciletti, Digital Design (ROM, PLA and PAL); Michael John Sebastian Smith, Application-Specific Integrated Circuits (programmable ASICs)."},
{s:OUT,k:'outro',term:'Outro',say:`So remember: drive, wait, then compare for test benches; the ${P('PLA')} shares its terms; and every lookup table holds two to the n bits. Next time, floorplanning, placement and routing. See you there!`,cues:{f:'So remember',w1:'drive, wait',w2:'shares its terms',w3:'and every lookup',n:'Next time',s:'See you there'},words:[['DRIVE, WAIT, COMPARE','BLU','w1'],['PLA SHARES TERMS','ORG','w2'],['2ⁿ BITS PER LUT','GRN','w3']],next:["NEXT TIME", "Next topic", "Floorplanning, placement and routing", "book"],end:'See you there!'}
